{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 8339 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "a4d7c5b06b46f3e638fc4993614a311286b098be80ca107dc6db3743abfcd292" :edb/db-before-t 8338 :edb/db-after-t 8339 :edb/tx-data [[13194139541651 50 #inst "2026-10-26T21:45:59.013Z" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1117 #edb/ref 17592186719476 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186049882 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186050057 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186045416 1118 #edb/ref 17592186050779 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719430 1064 "**MTH 255 — Recitation Worksheet 5**\n\nDue: 2026-10-29\nDue time: 11:59 p.m. PDT\nDeadline source: [Canvas — Week 5 Recitation Session](https://canvas.oregonstate.edu/courses/2064132/assignments/10705975), checked 2026-10-26; Canvas lists Thursday at 11:59 p.m.\nDate imported: 2026-10-26\nSource: [255-R5.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2F255-R5.pdf)\n\nStudy answers, explanations, and explicitly labeled reference sketches are independently authored additions. Source figures and problem statements are retained; domain and theorem-hypothesis qualifications are explained in the reveal fields.\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Complete all five problems and every labeled subpart. Show supporting work, including the requested sketches, proofs, and methods.\n- The PDF states that recitation worksheets are graded for completeness. Canvas describes attendance and participation grading and states that late work is not accepted.\n- Work on the printed template, write/type on the PDF with a tablet, or use your own paper with the same layout.\n- Upload one PDF to Gradescope under **Recitation Worksheet 5**. Preserve the six-page template format: a cover page followed by one page per problem, including any blank problems. If a problem uses multiple physical pages, combine them into one collage page for that problem. An incorrectly formatted PDF receives zero under the source instructions.\n- For regions with holes, use the entire positively oriented boundary: outer boundaries counterclockwise and inner boundaries clockwise. For flux, outward means outward from the shaded region, including into its holes." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719430 1066 #uuid "005a3768-8410-57e5-b534-802e52d24766" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719430 1067 "Assignment information" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719431 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719445 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719431 1071 "**(a)** Find the counterclockwise circulation of $\\mathbf F=\\langle-2y,3x\\rangle$ around the boundary of the shaded region. Include every boundary component or segment, with the region on the left.\n\n![Annular sector between radii 1 and 2, excluding the right-hand sector between y=-x and y=x](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fannular-sector-2a.png)\n\nCirculation: {{answer}}." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719431 1072 #uuid "0090f78f-b0b8-5835-9b37-323e92c257c8" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719431 1074 "The pictured region is $1\\le r\\le2$, $\\pi/4\\le\\theta\\le7\\pi/4$. Its angular width is $3\\pi/2$, so its area is $\\tfrac12(2^2-1^2)(3\\pi/2)=9\\pi/4$. The scalar curl is $\\partial_x(3x)-\\partial_y(-2y)=3+2=5$. Green's theorem gives circulation $5(9\\pi/4)=45\\pi/4$. The boundary includes the outer arc, two radial segments, and the inner arc in its opposite orientation." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719432 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719465 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719432 1062 #uuid "02e1326a-f503-5bca-994f-6dfa6bf7478d" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719432 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719483 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719433 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719453 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719433 1071 "**(c)** Show that on the right edge of $R$, $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=f(b)$." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719433 1072 #uuid "03a7f72f-b44a-5c0f-ab85-f67c045f2da6" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719433 1074 "The right edge has length one, $x=b$ is fixed, and the tangent points upward. A downward parametrization would have the wrong sign for the specified boundary orientation." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719440 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719434 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719434 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719434 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719440 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719434 1079 #uuid "04f73045-cd53-5ed1-a512-8b548add7cd5" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719435 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719439 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719435 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719488 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719435 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719502 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719435 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719504 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719435 1085 "Source: Problem 1(a–d), PDF page 2.\n\nFind the requested functions on the field's domain, noting any distinction between a local branch and a globally defined function. **Source hint:** There is a related problem in this week's written homework." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719435 1086 #uuid "0922e70e-242a-53d4-aed4-35319a95be31" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719435 1087 #edb/ref 17592186719439 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719436 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719461 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719436 1062 #uuid "0a42b551-d540-5382-a370-282b5a1f1b70" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719436 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719433 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719437 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719493 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719437 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719437 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719437 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719493 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719437 1079 #uuid "0a634087-b4ac-5ca2-8e59-3cd0853c52df" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719438 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719436 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719438 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719444 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719438 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719446 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719438 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719461 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719438 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719481 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719438 1085 "Source: Problem 4(a–e), PDF page 5.\n\nSuppose $f(x)$ is differentiable on $[a,b]$. Let\n\n$$R=[a,b]\\times[0,1]=\\{(x,y):a\\le x\\le b,\\ 0\\le y\\le1\\},\\qquad\\mathbf F=\\langle0,f(x)\\rangle.$$\n\nOrient the boundary of $R$ counterclockwise.\n\n![Rectangle R with x-coordinates a and b and height 1](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Frectangle-4.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719438 1086 #uuid "0cccca78-5ab8-5f7a-b657-e72e03bb81d8" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719438 1087 #edb/ref 17592186719446 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719439 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719488 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719439 1062 #uuid "10069bc2-91f3-52bb-8e56-ff3b1aa5b97b" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719439 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719499 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719440 1080 "12\\pi" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719440 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719440 1083 #uuid "1885cc85-a891-5979-809e-141f9623e009" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719441 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719455 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719441 1062 #uuid "1b453cd5-7e46-54e7-bb8b-bc19b7f1fc96" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719441 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719492 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719442 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719437 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719442 1071 "**(b)** Find the flux of $\\mathbf F=\\nabla\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$ out of the shaded region.\n\n![Annulus with inner radius 1 and outer radius 2](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fannulus-3b.png)\n\nOutward flux: {{answer}}." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719442 1072 #uuid "1f62ce36-36d9-5278-8736-218e35f12b54" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719442 1074 "For $r>0$, $\\mathbf F=(x/r,y/r)$ and $\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf F=1/r$. The origin is outside the annulus, so Green's theorem applies on this region:\n\n$$\\iint_R\\frac1r\\,dA=\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\int_1^2\\frac1r\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta=2\\pi.$$\n\nDirectly, the outer flux is $4\\pi$ and the inner flux is $-2\\pi$, giving $2\\pi$. Omitting the inner boundary would give the wrong answer." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719443 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719432 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719443 1062 #uuid "217d3c47-c519-527d-a4ec-442e4aab379a" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719443 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719430 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719444 1062 #uuid "25e150a9-5cb1-5147-bb81-e8c55c6572c6" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719444 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719487 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719445 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719466 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719445 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719445 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719445 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719466 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719445 1079 #uuid "351d661a-c568-5d01-89d7-7d83c416279b" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719446 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719481 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719446 1062 #uuid "364496c7-ecbe-5e33-98ce-7d9df4d65949" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719446 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719496 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719447 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719471 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719447 1071 "**(d)** For $\\mathbf F=\\left\\langle\\frac{-y}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle$, find a potential function $\\phi$ and a stream function $\\psi$. Draw a couple of equipotential curves and streamlines.\n\n![Source vector-field diagram](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Ffield-1d.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719447 1072 #uuid "396b73fa-e153-52a7-b857-cef12407f39e" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719447 1074 "Check $\\psi_y=-y/r^2=F_1$ and $-\\psi_x=x/r^2=F_2$. The field's unit-circle circulation is $2\\pi$, ruling out a global potential. A continuous angle branch works on a cut domain, for example $\\theta=\\arctan(y/x)$ on $x>0$. Additive constants in any valid potential or stream function do not change the field." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719448 1062 #uuid "401e76bf-c294-53dc-a64d-2bfd0d9e86df" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719448 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719494 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719449 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719450 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719449 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719449 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719449 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719450 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719449 1079 #uuid "458f209f-05f5-5241-98e9-84a208df632c" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719450 1080 "A potential is $\\phi=xy$, and a stream function is $\\psi=(y^2-x^2)/2$. Equipotentials satisfy $xy=c$; streamlines satisfy $y^2-x^2=2k$. Draw at least two curves of each family. The families meet orthogonally away from the stagnation point at the origin.\n\n**Authored reference sketch:**\n\n![Equipotentials and streamlines for part b](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fauthored-curves-1b.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719450 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719450 1083 #uuid "487d69a3-5107-500f-a294-5e368fd117e1" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719451 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719456 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719451 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719451 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719451 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719456 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719451 1079 #uuid "4e09c81b-8f8b-51d0-9506-bfe9be9debce" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719452 1062 #uuid "50086270-5023-523d-8aa7-8ec755f23fe9" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719452 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719497 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719459 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719453 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719453 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719453 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719459 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719453 1079 #uuid "54d42c6e-fe33-5b85-adc2-c6085a520af9" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719454 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719473 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719454 1062 #uuid "5d71f7bf-a32a-5963-b9cf-8fe1b0183278" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719454 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719431 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719455 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719448 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719455 1062 #uuid "624c509a-e950-59fb-a564-72ffec8b7ef6" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719455 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719477 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719456 1080 "8" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719456 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719456 1083 #uuid "64f0924c-0e12-51a7-af01-145e16e8fdb0" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719457 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719491 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719457 1071 "**(b)** Find the counterclockwise circulation of $\\mathbf F=\\langle0,xy\\rangle$ around the boundary of the shaded region.\n\n![Upper half-annulus between radii 1 and 2](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fupper-half-annulus-2b.png)\n\nCirculation: {{answer}}." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719457 1072 #uuid "6723d5bd-2fd9-5cdf-9e93-3864827f6161" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719457 1074 "Here $1\\le r\\le2$, $0\\le\\theta\\le\\pi$, and $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F=\\partial_x(xy)=y$. Hence\n\n$$\\oint_{\\partial R}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=\\iint_R y\\,dA=\\int_0^\\pi\\int_1^2 r^2\\sin\\theta\\,dr\\,d\\theta=\\frac73\\cdot2=\\frac{14}{3}.$$\n\nThe entire boundary is used, including the inner semicircle. The field is smooth on a neighborhood of the region." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719458 1080 "A potential is $\\phi=(x^2-y^2)/2$, and a stream function is $\\psi=xy$. Equipotentials satisfy $x^2-y^2=2c$; streamlines satisfy $xy=k$. Draw at least two curves of each family. Their regular intersections are orthogonal; the origin is a stagnation point.\n\n**Authored reference sketch:**\n\n![Equipotentials and streamlines for part a](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fauthored-curves-1a.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719458 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719458 1083 #uuid "678a02ec-f666-56ab-9f23-29e63201d943" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719459 1080 "The counterclockwise orientation traverses the right edge upward from $(b,0)$ to $(b,1)$. Parametrize it by $\\mathbf r(t)=(b,t)$, $0\\le t\\le1$. Then\n\n$$\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=\\int_0^1(0,f(b))\\cdot(0,1)\\,dt=f(b).$$" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719459 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719459 1083 #uuid "6b8da09c-3144-58f9-a42b-54e2421ef65f" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719480 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719460 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719460 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719460 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719480 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719460 1079 #uuid "6cbd8f99-fe20-5c85-aa8f-36cf039177e9" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719461 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719444 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719461 1062 #uuid "6ffd5fba-aae2-507f-9cf4-fd33b14c8446" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719461 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719468 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719462 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049084 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719462 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050332 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719462 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050560 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719462 1089 #edb/ref 17592186719472 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719462 1090 #uuid "73f97570-f6c5-59e5-b4fc-3be41ceb7f61" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719463 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719503 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719463 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719463 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719463 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719503 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719463 1079 #uuid "797ab717-31ad-5200-80d3-40e0eff47f89" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719464 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719505 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719464 1071 "**(b)** Show that on the top and bottom edges of $R$, the line integral $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds$ is zero." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719464 1072 #uuid "7caf2745-ec66-5f08-acba-1fbed834af52" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719464 1074 "The field is vertical, whereas the tangent to either horizontal edge is horizontal. Their dot product vanishes regardless of which horizontal edge is traversed left-to-right." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719465 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719441 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719465 1062 #uuid "7d56dda3-a715-599f-9474-916f403dfde1" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719465 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719462 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719466 1080 "\\frac{45\\pi}{4}" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719466 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719466 1083 #uuid "7d6d5af5-6fe8-5cff-8cde-744cf4bca8cb" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719467 1080 "Under Green's usual regularity hypotheses, for example if $f\\in C^1([a,b])$, the boundary calculation from (b–d) gives\n\n$$f(b)-f(a)=\\oint_{\\partial R}\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=\\iint_R f'(x)\\,dA=\\int_a^b\\int_0^1f'(x)\\,dy\\,dx=\\int_a^b f'(x)\\,dx.$$\n\nThis is the **Fundamental Theorem of Calculus**, in its Newton–Leibniz form.\n\nThe source assumes only that $f$ is differentiable. That alone does not ensure continuous first partial derivatives, as required by the standard version of Green's theorem used here; the formal derivation needs the additional regularity condition above (or an appropriate generalized theorem)." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719467 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719467 1083 #uuid "7f5f4c85-8d0a-5cbf-ad66-eb65561b455e" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719468 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719475 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719468 1071 "**(d)** Show that on the left edge of $R$, $\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=-f(a)$." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719468 1072 #uuid "80878db9-2bc3-5918-ad59-784bc38c3c1e" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719468 1074 "Counterclockwise traversal keeps the rectangle on the left. On the left edge this requires a downward tangent, accounting for the negative sign." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719469 1080 "A potential is locally $\\phi=\\theta=\\arg(x+iy)$ on a chosen angle branch; there is no single-valued global potential on the full punctured plane. A global stream function is $\\psi=-\\tfrac12\\ln(x^2+y^2)=-\\ln r$.\n\nLocal equipotentials are radial rays $\\theta=c$, and streamlines are circles $r=e^{-k}$ traversed counterclockwise. Draw a couple of rays and a couple of circles, excluding the origin.\n\n**Authored reference sketch:**\n\n![Equipotentials and streamlines for part d](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fauthored-curves-1d.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719469 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719469 1083 #uuid "8649c722-5aa8-51db-997f-16dc40aaf4af" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719470 1080 "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719470 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719470 1083 #uuid "8c24e57d-8218-50a7-8f39-98149bd36b89" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719469 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719471 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719471 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719471 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719469 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719471 1079 #uuid "8eee3749-21bf-5848-8c47-26f83fcbc9d4" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719472 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719454 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719472 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719473 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719472 1085 "Source: Problem 2(a–b), PDF page 3." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719472 1086 #uuid "8fa50f74-ea14-57c5-9cc7-9684c0dbd2ba" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719472 1087 #edb/ref 17592186719454 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719473 1062 #uuid "90ad2215-657b-5437-a146-71e22f69b2e8" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719473 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719457 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719474 1062 #uuid "92016bbe-4ac0-5e57-960f-b29a64fb7a2c" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719474 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719442 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719475 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719489 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719475 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719475 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719475 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719489 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719475 1079 #uuid "99d19a61-6d40-56fa-a974-3fee4ccc5bf6" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1043 #edb/ref 17592186719432 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1043 #edb/ref 17592186719441 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1043 #edb/ref 17592186719443 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1043 #edb/ref 17592186719448 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1043 #edb/ref 17592186719455 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1043 #edb/ref 17592186719465 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045461 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1045 "MTH 255 — R-5" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1046 #edb/ref 17592186719443 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1047 #inst "2026-10-30T06:59:00.000Z" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1048 #edb/ref 17592186405204 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719476 1053 #uuid "9bd6d23e-7bfe-5cbd-bb3d-ae38afb2d272" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719477 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049853 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719477 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050057 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719477 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050773 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719477 1088 #edb/ref 17592186051070 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719477 1088 #edb/ref 17592186051085 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719477 1089 #edb/ref 17592186719438 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719477 1090 #uuid "a05e3e51-bc65-5c0e-bc2f-2ca3a964d812" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719478 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719452 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719478 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719486 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719478 1085 "Source: Problem 5(a–b), PDF page 6.\n\nConsider the cardioid\n\n$$\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle\\cos t(1-\\sin t),\\ \\sin t(1-\\sin t)\\rangle,\\qquad0\\le t\\le2\\pi.$$\n\n![Source cardioid r=1-sin(t)](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fcardioid-5.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719478 1086 #uuid "a317f78d-2e52-59e3-a1f6-c0539bed7e46" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719478 1087 #edb/ref 17592186719486 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719479 1080 "\\frac{14}{3}" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719479 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719479 1083 #uuid "a53d3a8b-59b0-5ee4-bf47-61205da79458" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719480 1080 "f_{x}" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719480 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719480 1083 #uuid "b0c25130-9ad1-5acd-b4b5-3d1818d192dd" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719481 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719436 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719481 1062 #uuid "b6dc0994-fc54-5b98-94c3-9f3317bc7400" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719481 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719464 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719482 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719449 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719482 1071 "**(b)** For $\\mathbf F=\\langle y,x\\rangle$, find a potential function $\\phi$ and a stream function $\\psi$. Draw a couple of equipotential curves and streamlines.\n\n![Source vector-field diagram](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Ffield-1b.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719482 1072 #uuid "b7510f5f-cbaf-5458-b2ee-010c1ddc98af" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719482 1074 "Check $\\nabla\\phi=(y,x)$, $\\psi_y=y$, and $-\\psi_x=x$. The roles of the two hyperbola families are exchanged relative to part (a), with the indicated sign change in the stream function." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719483 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048308 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719483 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049617 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719483 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049882 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719483 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050869 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719483 1089 #edb/ref 17592186719435 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719483 1090 #uuid "b99fde82-6f0f-5c48-be1d-3c6a4617a234" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719484 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719458 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719484 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719484 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719484 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719458 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719484 1079 #uuid "bd86abe8-9fe0-5f81-b70e-916d5ea051fa" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719485 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719474 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719485 1062 #uuid "be1e5339-cb99-5543-95cf-22e44f3548af" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719485 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719498 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719486 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719452 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719486 1062 #uuid "c396a9eb-d20d-5351-9e9a-e6c0ececb5a3" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719486 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719490 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719487 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719507 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719487 1071 "**(e)** Apply the circulation form of Green's theorem to $\\mathbf F$ on $R$. What theorem do you get?" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719487 1072 #uuid "c4866e18-4bc1-5a67-be39-b6bc4d1e9f3a" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719487 1074 "Sum the four oriented edges first: $0+f(b)+0-f(a)$. The rectangle's height is one, so the double integral reduces directly to the one-variable integral. Do not claim the standard Green argument is justified by mere differentiability without addressing this hypothesis gap." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719488 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719502 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719488 1062 #uuid "c68bcd1e-f5a0-51e6-8c71-4227aaa6b2d1" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719488 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719482 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719489 1080 "The left edge is traversed downward from $(a,1)$ to $(a,0)$. Thus\n\n$$\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=\\int_1^0 f(a)\\,dy=-f(a).$$" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719489 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719489 1083 #uuid "cb1f9095-887a-5b33-be76-f21c24415e49" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719490 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719506 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719490 1071 "**(a)** Find the area enclosed by the cardioid. **Source hint:** Use Green's theorem with $\\mathbf F=\\langle0,x\\rangle$.\n\nArea: {{answer}}." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719490 1072 #uuid "cbd43edd-2d6a-5c69-a008-f7a6c7c2cfb5" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719490 1074 "For $\\mathbf F=(0,x)$, the scalar curl is $1$, so Green's theorem gives $A=\\oint_C x\\,dy$. Write $\\rho(t)=1-\\sin t$, $x=\\rho\\cos t$, and $y=\\rho\\sin t$. The traversal is counterclockwise. Since $\\oint_Cd(xy)=0$,\n\n$$A=\\frac12\\oint_C(x\\,dy-y\\,dx)=\\frac12\\int_0^{2\\pi}\\rho(t)^2\\,dt.$$\n\nHere $xy'-yx'=\\rho^2$, so\n\n$$A=\\frac12\\int_0^{2\\pi}(1-2\\sin t+\\sin^2t)\\,dt=\\frac12(2\\pi+\\pi)=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}.$$\n\nThis derives the polar-area expression from the requested Green's-theorem field rather than substituting a different required method." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719491 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719479 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719491 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719491 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719491 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719479 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719491 1079 #uuid "cd6a9e3a-5016-57c4-8f06-962ad56b5407" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719492 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049084 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719492 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049459 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719492 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050560 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719492 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050694 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719492 1089 #edb/ref 17592186719500 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719492 1090 #uuid "cff8335e-1063-50d1-93e0-c2731efe6d54" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719493 1080 "2\\pi" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719493 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719493 1083 #uuid "d1125f9f-1f50-5c19-9257-ed8ca212b368" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719494 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049853 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719494 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050567 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719494 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050779 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719494 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050860 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719494 1089 #edb/ref 17592186719478 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719494 1090 #uuid "d1bbccb8-57fc-5259-9e3b-6dc3b0164398" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719495 1080 "On either horizontal edge, $dy=0$. Since $\\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf T\\,ds=P\\,dx+Q\\,dy=0\\,dx+f(x)\\,dy$, the integrand is zero. Thus the integral along each of the top and bottom edges is zero." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719495 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719495 1083 #uuid "d469e5c0-77c8-51f1-ba34-7ee6ba184feb" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719496 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719460 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719496 1071 "**(a)** Find $\\operatorname{curl}\\mathbf F$. Use derivative-subscript notation in the answer.\n\nScalar curl: {{answer}}." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719496 1072 #uuid "d4d18464-6bd9-506f-8c72-09a6410dde12" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719496 1074 "For $\\mathbf F=(P,Q)=(0,f(x))$, the planar scalar curl is $Q_x-P_y=f_x-0=f_x$, where $f_x=f'(x)$ for the one-variable function $f$." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719497 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719451 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719497 1071 "**(b)** Find the arc length of the cardioid.\n\n**Source hint:**\n\n$$\\sqrt{1-\\sin t}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-\\sin t}\\sqrt{1+\\sin t}}{\\sqrt{1+\\sin t}}=\\frac{|\\cos t|}{\\sqrt{1+\\sin t}}.$$\n\nArc length: {{answer}}." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719497 1072 #uuid "d804dc20-c6fb-53e1-8c66-8b204ed8bbc7" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719497 1074 "With $\\rho=1-\\sin t$ and $\\rho'=-\\cos t$, the speed satisfies\n\n$$\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|=\\sqrt{(\\rho')^2+\\rho^2}=\\sqrt{\\cos^2t+(1-\\sin t)^2}=\\sqrt{2(1-\\sin t)}.$$\n\nUsing the supplied hint, split where $\\cos t$ changes sign: $t=\\pi/2$ and $3\\pi/2$. On the three resulting intervals, integrate $\\sqrt2|\\cos t|/\\sqrt{1+\\sin t}$ to obtain respectively $4-2\\sqrt2$, $4$, and $2\\sqrt2$. Their sum is $8$.\n\nThe quotient in the hint is undefined at $t=3\\pi/2$, even though the original speed is defined there; use the continuous limiting value in this intermediate expression. Alternatively, the identity $\\sqrt{2(1-\\sin t)}=2|\\sin(t/2-\\pi/4)|$ yields the same total length." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719498 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719434 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719498 1071 "**(a)** Find the flux of $\\mathbf F=\\nabla(x^2+y^2)$ out of the shaded region.\n\n![Annulus with inner radius 1 and outer radius 2](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fannulus-3a.png)\n\nOutward flux: {{answer}}." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719498 1072 #uuid "de548bef-88d0-5a3d-b4d8-48dc735f22f5" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719498 1074 "The field is $\\mathbf F=(2x,2y)$, with divergence $2+2=4$. The annulus has area $\\pi(2^2-1^2)=3\\pi$, so the flux form of Green's theorem gives $4(3\\pi)=12\\pi$. Independently, the outer-circle flux is $4\\cdot4\\pi=16\\pi$, and the inner-circle flux is $(-2)\\cdot2\\pi=-4\\pi$, since outward from the annulus points toward the hole there. Their sum is $12\\pi$." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719499 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719484 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719499 1071 "**(a)** For $\\mathbf F=\\langle x,-y\\rangle$, find a potential function $\\phi$ and a stream function $\\psi$. Draw a couple of equipotential curves and streamlines.\n\n![Source vector-field diagram](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Ffield-1a.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719499 1072 #uuid "df77f345-f20c-5f14-b98c-110b1ed20f2a" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719499 1074 "Check $\\nabla\\phi=(x,-y)$, $\\psi_y=x$, and $-\\psi_x=-y$. The potential curves are hyperbolas opening along the coordinate axes, while the streamlines are rectangular hyperbolas with the coordinate axes as their zero-level components." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719500 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719474 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719500 1084 #edb/ref 17592186719485 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719500 1085 "Source: Problem 3(a–b), PDF page 4." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719500 1086 #uuid "e5b2bfad-c83c-57c1-8b1b-52629c2657a6" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719500 1087 #edb/ref 17592186719485 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719501 1068 #edb/ref 17592186719463 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719501 1071 "**(c)** For $\\mathbf F=\\left\\langle\\frac{x}{x^2+y^2},\\frac{y}{x^2+y^2}\\right\\rangle$, find a potential function $\\phi$ and a stream function $\\psi$. Draw a couple of equipotential curves and streamlines.\n\n![Source vector-field diagram](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Ffield-1c.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719501 1072 #uuid "e5c996e0-6d97-56e4-b860-1a7299c3faf3" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719501 1074 "The field is undefined at the origin. Locally, $\\theta_x=-y/r^2$ and $\\theta_y=x/r^2$, so $\\psi_y=F_1$ and $-\\psi_x=F_2$. If a global stream function existed, its gradient would be $(-y/r^2,x/r^2)$, whose circulation around the unit circle is $2\\pi$, impossible for a gradient. Circle and ray families still describe equipotentials and streamlines geometrically." 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719502 1058 #edb/ref 17592186719504 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719502 1062 #uuid "e7e421b6-eaae-5375-bff7-1743892af67a" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719502 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719501 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719503 1080 "On the punctured plane, $\\phi=\\tfrac12\\ln(x^2+y^2)=\\ln r$ is a global potential. A stream function is locally $\\psi=\\theta=\\arg(x+iy)$ after choosing an angle branch. No single-valued global stream function exists on the full punctured plane.\n\nEquipotentials are circles $r=e^c$; streamlines are outward radial rays $\\theta=k$. Draw a couple of circles and a couple of rays, excluding the origin.\n\n**Authored reference sketch:**\n\n![Equipotentials and streamlines for part c](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fauthored-curves-1c.png)" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719503 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719503 1083 #uuid "e8acfb86-65b6-5e64-a923-778070420c77" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719504 1062 #uuid "ea5b9c0c-cc7c-5b49-a6a9-706bc8166140" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719504 1063 #edb/ref 17592186719447 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719505 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719495 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719505 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719505 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719505 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719495 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719505 1079 #uuid "f3eb20ba-2856-5c6d-bb39-77a2afde1460" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719506 1075 #edb/ref 17592186719470 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719506 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719506 1077 "answer" 13194139541651 17592186502323 true] [17592186719506 1078 #edb/ref 17592186719470 1319413954